# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MT-1 verification tooling — see docs/evidence/README.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `tests/mt1-rules-matrix.mjs` is the emulator-only (demo project) Firestore
# Rules matrix runner. It needs no production credentials, so it IS tracked and
# is wired to `npm run test:mt1:rules`.
#
# Every other MT-1 script is a production probe: it needs live Firebase
# credentials, a deployed origin, or a real Edge/CDP browser session. Those must
# never execute in CI and are deliberately outside the tracked baseline. They
# remain on disk as Step 2 tooling and are ignored here so the tracked tree stays
# clean.
tests/mt1-api-read.mjs
tests/mt1-browser-e2e.mjs
tests/mt1-cdp-evidence.mjs
tests/mt1-deployed-read.mjs
tests/mt1-local-dom.mjs
tests/mt1-token-probe.mjs

# The emulator suites above rewrite their own evidence file on every run, so a
# tracked copy could only ever be stale and would dirty the working tree after
# each `npm run test:local`. CI uploads them as the `emulator-evidence` artifact.
docs/evidence/mt1-matrix-evidence.txt
docs/evidence/password-setup-ordering-evidence.txt

# Windows reserved device name. A leaked Auth credential artifact was previously
# created under this name (`> nul` inside a non-cmd shell); never allow it back
# into the tree.
nul
